    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4487" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">augŭrātus</span></b> ,
		ūs, m.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The office of augur.</i> auguratus alicujus, <i><span class="en">Cic.
				Vatin. 9</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insigne auguratūs,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Div. 1, 17, 30</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scientia auguratūs,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib.</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">auguratu praeditus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					1, 62</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">auguratum accipere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 4, 8, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> =
			augurium, <i>augury</i>, <i><span class="en">Tert.
				Anim. 26</span></i>.</div>
